## 5. Verdict - Does V8 Need an Update?

### Short answer

**No methodological rewrite. Minor citation/update addendum is advisable.**

| Dimension | V8 status | New evidence | Action |
|---|---|---|---|
| Threat model / guardrail mechanism | `_extract_target` first-present-key blind spot + taint 5 superset 2 verified in S4.1/S8 | **Confirmed independently** twice: `tapiwamakandigona` 34.385 vs 0.000 A/B and `seb001010` + `ahmedmobasher86` asymmetry notes | **Add citations.** Insert 1-line credit + 1-line distinction (minimal proof vs throughput ceiling) in S8/S11. V8 self-test already proves same (`tools/local_test.py:297-313`). |
| Throughput ceiling | 91-92.5 band, v64 92.540 peak, 20 post-v64 failures (<5pts=noise), top-50 cutoff 111.690 | No Sept 1+ title claims > ~60 or new vote-leader >30 that beats 92.540; highest-vote Sept item is 12 (antoniorotundo2) framed as throughput floor | **No change.** Could append antoniorotundo2 + takamichitoda raw per second as convergent support in S7 Table W-E2. |
| Private LB thesis (0.07 median, deputy wins) | Private 0.210 best (v76), winner Xz 46.425 taint-free `email.send` | New Sept private datapoint `municef1` 22.155 deputy and `takamichitoda` clean deputy survivor match thesis; `yw8837` 34->8 collapse mirrors it | **Add 1 row** to S6.4 Table 5 (municef1 22.155) as lower-deputy proof. Reinforces, does not contradict. |
| Defense checklist (S8 Lessons / S9 Usefulness) | 4 lessons: match all args, sticky taint, taint every channel, judge vs flexible agent | Real-world Sept vectors (GhostJacking log-as-injection, module shadowing) map to treat logs as untrusted + isolate reasoning channel | **Optional 2-sentence bridge** in S8 noting production-harness vectors as out-of-benchmark example of same channel-confusion class. Keep scope box intact. |
| Figure / repro methodology | 4 figures deterministic from `scoring.py` + recorded scores | `hexisteme/aisec-wn-figures` `make_figures.py` independent same class | **No figure regeneration needed.** Cite as parallel figure-repro if style requests. |

### Concrete edit checklist if we do a V8.1 addendum (est. ~30 mins, no reruns)

- [ ] S8 + S11: add `tapiwamakandigona/kaggle-agent-security/WORKING_NOTE.md` (argument shadowing 34.385 vs 0.000) - credit as **independent replication of S4.1 blind spot**; distinction: tapiwamakandigona isolates mechanism with minimal burst; V8 isolates ceiling with throughput-first search (Harmony + halving + fill).
- [ ] S6.4 Table 5: append `municef1` 22.155 deputy as lower-deputy private proof; optionally cite `yw8837` 34->8 as small-scale collapse.
- [ ] S7 Table 6 family F8/F9 notes: cross-ref `takamichitoda` clean CONFUSED_DEPUTY survivor + `antoniorotundo2` throughput-floor as convergent evidence hedge must be large and search cheap.
- [ ] S8 Lessons: add 2-line Production-harness parallel (Sep 2026) box citing GhostJacking (Adversa 2026-09-03, 90pct Claude Code) as log-as-injection cousin.
- [ ] Appendix Sept ledger: paste S4 table (38 rows) as Table V8-S1 so reviewers see V8 weighed all 810 + tracked Sept tail to 2026-09-04T18:38 (deadline 2026-09-08).
- [ ] No score-table, figure, or `src/` change required; `tools/local_test.py` 60-s self-test still falsifies blind spot locally.

### What would force a real rewrite (not triggered)

- A Sept 1+ kernel with public > ~105 or private > ~30 deputy beating Xz pattern with transferable technique V8 race/fill cannot emulate (e.g., new private-survivable predicate or wall-clock exploit beyond THS). None appears in this sweep - title/vote/replay-wall signals are flat or supportive.

